Overview

The New Ballard Score (NBS) is a postnatal clinical assessment method used to estimate gestational age by evaluating a newborn's neuromuscular and physical maturity.

This repository provides an educational resource for neonatal nurses, midwives, pediatricians, nursing students, and other healthcare professionals interested in structured newborn assessment and clinical documentation.

The guide covers all 12 maturity criteria, scoring principles, gestational-age estimation, practical considerations, and an accompanying printable assessment worksheet.

«Clinical notice: This repository is intended for educational purposes. The accompanying worksheet is an educational draft, not a validated or institutionally approved clinical instrument. Verify all scoring descriptions, illustrations, and conversion values against the original New Ballard Score instrument before clinical use. Follow your institution's approved neonatal assessment protocol.»

